# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# EAS archives from the git root to support monorepos, so an Expo build was
# shipping admin/ (1.1 GB) and web/ (680 MB) along with it — a 689 MB tarball
# for an app that needs neither. Two production uploads died mid-transfer with
# write EPIPE (at 98 MB and 147 MB) before this file existed.
#
# Everything excluded here is either reinstalled or regenerated on the build
# server, or belongs to a different app:
#   node_modules  — reinstalled from the lockfile, which is NOT excluded
#   expo/ios, expo/android — regenerated by prebuild; both are gitignored and
#                            untracked, so they are build output, not source
#   expo/dist     — local export output
#   admin/, web/  — separate applications, not imported by the mobile app
#
# Do not add source directories here. If a build starts failing on a missing
# file, this is the first place to look.

node_modules/
**/node_modules/

admin/
web/
supabase/
artifacts/
tmp/

expo/ios/
expo/android/
expo/dist/
expo/.expo/

# Build-time values come from the EAS environment. Never upload local env or
# signing material, even when a local file currently contains public-only keys.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
**/credentials/

.git/
docs/
scripts/
supabase/tests/

**/.DS_Store
*.aab
*.apk
*.apks
*.ipa
*.xcarchive/
